WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.470
- There's been so much stress and anxiety

00:00:02.470 --> 00:00:04.474
and negativity around this election

00:00:04.474 --> 00:00:06.617
and I think it's having
a real impact on me

00:00:06.617 --> 00:00:08.318
and my emotional well-being.

00:00:08.318 --> 00:00:11.429
So I just wanna take that
energy, that negativity,

00:00:11.429 --> 00:00:12.664
and turn it into something positive

00:00:12.664 --> 00:00:15.586
and go out there and do
something useful with my time.

00:00:15.586 --> 00:00:18.503
(soft piano music)

00:00:20.308 --> 00:00:22.986
- This weekend, we are going to go canvas

00:00:22.986 --> 00:00:26.494
in Nevada for Hillary Rodham Clinton.

00:00:26.494 --> 00:00:29.054
This election has been crazy

00:00:29.054 --> 00:00:31.137
and I feel a lot of fear.

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:35.630
One of the ways that I can
feel better about what happens

00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.372
on Tuesday is knowing that
this weekend I made an effort

00:00:38.372 --> 00:00:39.307
to help get out the vote.

00:00:39.307 --> 00:00:41.899
- This campaign was weird
because young people

00:00:41.899 --> 00:00:44.547
and people my age were less
politically active than usual

00:00:44.547 --> 00:00:46.978
and I feel like I sort of
subscribed to that as well,

00:00:46.978 --> 00:00:48.820
but as we get closer and
closer to the reality

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.680
that Donald Trump might become president

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.107
I am definitely feeling more
of an urge to get involved.

00:00:53.107 --> 00:00:55.896
- When I graduated college I
became a community organizer

00:00:55.896 --> 00:00:58.476
and now it's crunch time.

00:00:58.476 --> 00:01:01.660
- My expectations for
tomorrow are to be very tired

00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:03.212
and very frustrated.

00:01:03.212 --> 00:01:04.045
- It's a swing state,

00:01:04.045 --> 00:01:06.916
so they've been getting a
lot of people calling them,

00:01:06.916 --> 00:01:08.683
a lot of people knocking on their doors.

00:01:08.683 --> 00:01:10.342
- We're gonna drive four
hours, we're gonna talk

00:01:10.342 --> 00:01:12.428
to a lot of people who
will probably yell at us,

00:01:12.428 --> 00:01:14.537
and then we're gonna drive
four hours back to LA.

00:01:14.537 --> 00:01:15.736
- So let's go, let's do it!

00:01:15.736 --> 00:01:17.221
- Nevada, here we come.

00:01:17.221 --> 00:01:21.873
- So, I'm awake and the
sun is not even up yet.

00:01:21.873 --> 00:01:24.505
- I really don't want to go,
I just wanna go back to bed.

00:01:24.505 --> 00:01:25.338
- HRC,

00:01:26.396 --> 00:01:27.309
fully repping.

00:01:27.309 --> 00:01:29.115
- I'm secretly hoping
that nobody shows up.

00:01:29.115 --> 00:01:31.634
- Gonna go save America,
gonna go do our duty.

00:01:31.634 --> 00:01:33.717
We're on the road, going.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:35.815
- Getting excited.

00:01:35.815 --> 00:01:37.089
- Woo, go Hillary!

00:01:37.089 --> 00:01:40.239
- We're here in the office in Nevada.

00:01:40.239 --> 00:01:43.698
- Someone has made an
amazing mural behind me.

00:01:43.698 --> 00:01:44.600
This office is dope.

00:01:44.600 --> 00:01:47.350
- And I even met Hillary Clinton.

00:01:48.898 --> 00:01:50.663
She's happy 'cause she
knows she's gonna win.

00:01:50.663 --> 00:01:52.916
We just got our packets and
we're gonna head out to canvas.

00:01:52.916 --> 00:01:54.700
I'm a little nervous.

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.934
We'll be talking to democrats

00:01:55.934 --> 00:01:57.616
and just convincing
people to get out to vote.

00:01:57.616 --> 00:02:00.016
- Already with her, with her, with her.

00:02:00.016 --> 00:02:02.106
- We're at a house right now
where we just got trained

00:02:02.106 --> 00:02:04.934
by someone who walked us through
what we're supposed to say.

00:02:04.934 --> 00:02:06.949
It's very overwhelming,
we just heard it once

00:02:06.949 --> 00:02:09.164
and now we just go out
and say it to people.

00:02:09.164 --> 00:02:11.033
- We just got our walk packets.

00:02:11.033 --> 00:02:13.826
The organizer in me is already
(bang drowns out speaker)

00:02:13.826 --> 00:02:15.969
how to tear them up, make
it the most efficient.

00:02:15.969 --> 00:02:17.923
- Okay, well, we're in
the suburbs of Las Vegas

00:02:17.923 --> 00:02:18.756
and we're about to start.

00:02:18.756 --> 00:02:20.917
I feel like once I get
a couple houses down,

00:02:20.917 --> 00:02:23.314
I'll get the rhythm of it, but
right now, yeah, it's scary.

00:02:23.314 --> 00:02:25.020
- We just knocked out our first street.

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.405
I talked to one person who was like,

00:02:26.405 --> 00:02:28.092
"Yeah, I'm definitely a Republican."

00:02:28.092 --> 00:02:29.084
On to the next street.

00:02:29.084 --> 00:02:31.366
- I'm feeling pretty
bad because I just went

00:02:31.366 --> 00:02:34.485
to five or six houses
and no one was there.

00:02:34.485 --> 00:02:36.277
Someone sort of made fun of me.

00:02:36.277 --> 00:02:38.711
Sort of made me feel like,
man, we drove all the way here.

00:02:38.711 --> 00:02:40.126
Is this a good use of our time?

00:02:40.126 --> 00:02:41.582
- Just knocked on the door of someone who

00:02:41.582 --> 00:02:43.291
is having a baby shower.

00:02:43.291 --> 00:02:45.961
I was standing at the door
and I was hearing them clap

00:02:45.961 --> 00:02:48.321
and cheer and I just couldn't do it.

00:02:48.321 --> 00:02:50.697
So I chickened out and
now I'm regretting it

00:02:50.697 --> 00:02:52.646
because there were so many conversations

00:02:52.646 --> 00:02:54.019
to be had about voting.

00:02:54.019 --> 00:02:56.449
- Just talked to somebody
who was a Hillary supporter

00:02:56.449 --> 00:02:58.467
and said she was gonna go vote on Tuesday.

00:02:58.467 --> 00:02:59.343
She knew where she was voting.

00:02:59.343 --> 00:03:01.502
She was really enthusiastic
and supportive of us,

00:03:01.502 --> 00:03:02.524
so that felt really good.

00:03:02.524 --> 00:03:04.265
- Just had an amazing conversation

00:03:04.265 --> 00:03:06.343
with a very sweet lady named Maria.

00:03:06.343 --> 00:03:07.981
Got through the whole script with her.

00:03:07.981 --> 00:03:09.447
She was like, "Yes I am voting."

00:03:09.447 --> 00:03:10.405
I was like, "Great.

00:03:10.405 --> 00:03:11.659
"Do you know where your polling place is?

00:03:11.659 --> 00:03:12.856
"How are you gonna get to the polls?

00:03:12.856 --> 00:03:14.198
"Do you know what time you're going?"

00:03:14.198 --> 00:03:15.341
She's got a voting plan.

00:03:15.341 --> 00:03:16.908
- We're probably about 10 houses deep

00:03:16.908 --> 00:03:18.673
and I'm actually having fun.

00:03:18.673 --> 00:03:19.997
Every house is a new adventure.

00:03:19.997 --> 00:03:21.586
- I am crying human tears.

00:03:21.586 --> 00:03:24.385
I just talked to a lady
who definitely was not

00:03:24.385 --> 00:03:27.175
in the place where she wanted
to talk about anything,

00:03:27.175 --> 00:03:29.663
and especially not with
a stranger who was coming

00:03:29.663 --> 00:03:32.519
to talk to her about an election
she is pissed off about.

00:03:32.519 --> 00:03:35.908
By the end of the conversation
she was so just more open.

00:03:35.908 --> 00:03:38.587
We talked about how important Nevada is,

00:03:38.587 --> 00:03:40.289
how much her voice counts here,

00:03:40.289 --> 00:03:44.123
and left that experience just
feeling humbled and emotional.

00:03:44.123 --> 00:03:46.129
Glad that I was able to have
such a meaningful conversation

00:03:46.129 --> 00:03:46.962
with someone today.

00:03:46.962 --> 00:03:48.652
- We've been walking for three hours now

00:03:48.652 --> 00:03:50.586
and my legs are so fucking tired.

00:03:50.586 --> 00:03:52.978
My whole body is exhausted,
but it feels good.

00:03:52.978 --> 00:03:53.988
I wanna keep going.

00:03:53.988 --> 00:03:56.977
I just talked to somebody who
said she was going to vote

00:03:56.977 --> 00:03:58.575
but she didn't know who yet.

00:03:58.575 --> 00:03:59.808
We had a little bit of a conversation.

00:03:59.808 --> 00:04:01.245
I'm not sure if she wanted to be swayed.

00:04:01.245 --> 00:04:02.362
I'm not sure if I did sway her,

00:04:02.362 --> 00:04:04.405
but hopefully she'll
think about her decision.

00:04:04.405 --> 00:04:06.365
- [Alaina] This is the polling place

00:04:06.365 --> 00:04:08.460
that we've been talking about.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:10.158
A convenient walk away.

00:04:10.158 --> 00:04:12.067
Look how freakin' beautiful it is.

00:04:12.067 --> 00:04:13.187
- Nevada is so tight right now.

00:04:13.187 --> 00:04:16.384
Hillary Clinton's at
49% and Trump is at 50.

00:04:16.384 --> 00:04:18.681
So I feel like we are making a difference

00:04:18.681 --> 00:04:19.926
and our presence here matters.

00:04:19.926 --> 00:04:21.304
It was worth getting
out of bed this morning.

00:04:21.304 --> 00:04:22.540
- Even if people aren't on your list

00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:24.131
you're kind of interacting with them.

00:04:24.131 --> 00:04:26.148
There's like all these
kids around right now

00:04:26.148 --> 00:04:27.499
and they're very interested like,

00:04:27.499 --> 00:04:28.635
"What are you doing, what are you doing?"

00:04:28.635 --> 00:04:31.219
and I was like, "Yeah, I'm
just a neighbor coming around

00:04:31.219 --> 00:04:33.090
"to make sure all your
parents are ready to vote.

00:04:33.090 --> 00:04:34.544
"Can you talk to them for me?

00:04:34.544 --> 00:04:35.377
"Make sure they are."

00:04:35.377 --> 00:04:38.009
And this one girl was like,
"Yeah, Hillary Clinton!"

00:04:38.009 --> 00:04:39.829
- It's funny because out here you realize

00:04:39.829 --> 00:04:41.280
that you're like a face of the campaign

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.417
and you really do wanna
be nice to everybody

00:04:43.417 --> 00:04:45.011
and even people who disagree with you.

00:04:45.011 --> 00:04:46.450
- There was a bunch of
people just sitting around

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:47.283
in a driveway.

00:04:47.283 --> 00:04:49.036
I could hear them as I was
walking away being like,

00:04:49.036 --> 00:04:50.309
"Did you vote yet?"

00:04:50.309 --> 00:04:52.203
And just knowing that my presence

00:04:52.203 --> 00:04:54.800
is stimulating those
conversations is super cool.

00:04:54.800 --> 00:04:57.579
- This process is just
making it so clear to me

00:04:57.579 --> 00:05:01.268
how personal this is and
how every vote does matter.

00:05:01.268 --> 00:05:03.908
I just knocked on the door
and it was this Latina woman

00:05:03.908 --> 00:05:06.718
and she said she's been watching
the election on the news

00:05:06.718 --> 00:05:09.009
and she can't take it anymore
and she doesn't wanna vote,

00:05:09.009 --> 00:05:11.122
and it was really upsetting that someone

00:05:11.122 --> 00:05:12.368
who normally would vote democratic

00:05:12.368 --> 00:05:13.603
just didn't wanna vote at all.

00:05:13.603 --> 00:05:15.693
We tried talking to her and
she became sort of interested.

00:05:15.693 --> 00:05:17.126
She was like, "What times
do the polls close?"

00:05:17.126 --> 00:05:17.991
Maybe she'll go out.

00:05:17.991 --> 00:05:20.175
But it was heartbreaking
because as we were saying,

00:05:20.175 --> 00:05:22.372
"This is a swing state,
your vote really matters"

00:05:22.372 --> 00:05:24.504
her daughter was shouting,
"Hillary Clinton!

00:05:24.504 --> 00:05:25.337
"Hillary Clinton!"

00:05:25.337 --> 00:05:27.344
And I wanted to be like,
"Listen to your daughter.

00:05:27.344 --> 00:05:29.261
"She wants to see Hillary
Clinton in the White House.

00:05:29.261 --> 00:05:30.746
"She wants to see a woman
in the White House."

00:05:30.746 --> 00:05:32.010
I really hope that woman votes.

00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.509
I thought everyone would be mean to me.

00:05:33.509 --> 00:05:34.856
A couple people were mean to me,

00:05:34.856 --> 00:05:36.722
but so many people just wanna talk to you

00:05:36.722 --> 00:05:38.553
and wanna discuss issues with you.

00:05:38.553 --> 00:05:39.609
It's been really heartening.

00:05:39.609 --> 00:05:41.446
- It's getting pretty dark out.

00:05:41.446 --> 00:05:43.193
- At the beginning of the
night I was so nervous

00:05:43.193 --> 00:05:44.937
and at this point I just wanna keep going.

00:05:44.937 --> 00:05:46.805
I feel fearless ringing on doors.

00:05:46.805 --> 00:05:48.523
I could talk to a million people tonight.

00:05:48.523 --> 00:05:51.008
Had this amazing
conversation with this woman

00:05:51.008 --> 00:05:54.035
who was very excited to vote,
very excited about Hillary,

00:05:54.035 --> 00:05:55.338
and then I met her husband

00:05:55.338 --> 00:05:58.305
who was similarly excited about Hillary

00:05:58.305 --> 00:06:01.191
but he was a felon and he couldn't vote.

00:06:01.191 --> 00:06:03.781
He was very informed, he knew
who he wanted to vote for.

00:06:03.781 --> 00:06:05.055
Then it was really hard to see

00:06:05.055 --> 00:06:07.195
that he couldn't exercise
his right that he had.

00:06:07.195 --> 00:06:10.101
- Just had an awesome
conversation with a lady

00:06:10.101 --> 00:06:12.247
who recently moved to this house.

00:06:12.247 --> 00:06:13.466
She's not registered here,

00:06:13.466 --> 00:06:14.942
she's registered at her last location,

00:06:14.942 --> 00:06:17.238
so we made sure that she was heading

00:06:17.238 --> 00:06:18.675
to her old polling location.

00:06:18.675 --> 00:06:20.755
Just making sure those
logistics were in place.

00:06:20.755 --> 00:06:22.771
- Overall, it's been a
really worthwhile experience

00:06:22.771 --> 00:06:24.367
and it makes me wanna get involved more.

00:06:24.367 --> 00:06:25.807
I wanna do phone banking,

00:06:25.807 --> 00:06:27.191
make sure everyone gets out to vote.

00:06:27.191 --> 00:06:29.369
- We're wrapping up just
a couple more houses.

00:06:29.369 --> 00:06:32.207
Really tired, ready to go
home, but let's finish this up.

00:06:32.207 --> 00:06:34.836
- I was so tired when I
got back I just collapsed

00:06:34.836 --> 00:06:37.520
into my bed and I felt
so happy to have gone.

00:06:37.520 --> 00:06:39.856
It was like a 180 from
how I felt that morning.

00:06:39.856 --> 00:06:41.916
There were some conversations
where I really did feel

00:06:41.916 --> 00:06:44.237
that their opinions had
changed a little bit.

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:46.243
They were more likely to
get out there and vote,

00:06:46.243 --> 00:06:48.443
and that's so cool and powerful.

00:06:48.443 --> 00:06:49.425
- I'm so glad we went.

00:06:49.425 --> 00:06:50.953
It has been an election

00:06:50.953 --> 00:06:53.556
where a lot of us have felt helpless,

00:06:53.556 --> 00:06:56.205
and I forgot that being active

00:06:56.205 --> 00:06:59.205
makes you feel so much more involved

00:07:00.040 --> 00:07:01.793
and able to do something.

00:07:01.793 --> 00:07:03.624
- I definitely feel a different sort

00:07:03.624 --> 00:07:05.405
of investment when I
look at these numbers.

00:07:05.405 --> 00:07:07.957
I feel that I can do
something to change them.

00:07:07.957 --> 00:07:09.400
We have to do better, we can do better,

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:12.152
and I feel the sense of
wanting to participate.

00:07:12.152 --> 00:07:14.617
- There isn't anything
that replaces that feeling

00:07:14.617 --> 00:07:17.248
of making a difference in your community.

00:07:17.248 --> 00:07:19.427
- Showing up at someone's
door and being able to listen

00:07:19.427 --> 00:07:22.310
to what's affecting their
lives is really important

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:24.328
to the political process
and really important

00:07:24.328 --> 00:07:27.244
to my life as a person
who lives in this country

00:07:27.244 --> 00:07:29.358
and wants to improve the country.

00:07:29.358 --> 00:07:30.978
- There is nothing I would've rather done

00:07:30.978 --> 00:07:32.395
the weekend before the election

00:07:32.395 --> 00:07:35.312
than knock doors in a swing state.

